# RetroPaint

RetroPaint is a tactile kids' paint app. Keep the chunky neo-brutalist UI and synthesized sounds. Every tool and ink is available from the start.

- Boot onto a ready canvas. No login, accounts, splash gate, skill levels, or switch-scan mode.
- Options use illustrated buttons with readable labels. Popups never scroll: group choices into categories and fit the panel to the viewport. The canvas fills the space left after the tool bin, top bar, and material tray are laid out.
- Save downloads a PNG picture. There is no movie export.
- Gradients appear only while the bucket is selected. Rainbow ink is always distance-based.
- Applicators (how paint lands) stay separate from inks (what paint is).
- Canvas logic lives in `src/` modules. Do not collapse the app back into one HTML file.

```ts
// ❌ one mega script in index.html
// ✅ src/draw.ts applies the active applicator + ink
```
